  "term": "preparedness",
  "definition": "Preparedness is the readiness and ability of individuals, households, and communities to respond effectively to a pandemic. It includes practical elements such as having essential supplies, resources, and backup plans, and people’s sense of being prepared can affect stress and other mental health outcomes.",
